WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.196
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.466 --> 00:04.221
Your selfish feelings

3
00:04.221 --> 00:07.173
robbed me of the job I loved.

4
00:07.173 --> 00:09.185
Goodbye.

5
00:09.185 --> 00:11.266
I don't think we'll ever meet again.

6
00:16.245 --> 00:20.589
My love stole O-Con's love.

7
00:23.777 --> 00:27.600
What? Did you actually take that seriously?

8
00:30.501 --> 00:32.741
I mean, even with all your aggressive advances,

9
00:32.741 --> 00:37.205
did Ms. Kusakabe ever look genuinely disgusted or creeped out?

10
00:37.205 --> 00:38.761
No.

11
00:38.761 --> 00:41.053
But I'm her employer, so in front of me...

12
00:41.053 --> 00:44.633
She never acted like that in front of us either.

13
00:45.485 --> 00:46.845
Then why?

14
00:46.845 --> 00:49.185
- Why say something so harsh to me? - Most likely,

15
00:49.185 --> 00:51.021
it was for Tuesla's sake.

16
00:51.021 --> 00:54.121
- Tuesla? - Just like you and Mr. Omishima,

17
00:54.121 --> 00:56.833
Ms. Kusakabe is facing a big scandal right now.

18
00:58.525 --> 01:00.233
[Arrest the Home Wrecker! Ms. Kusakabe Only Cares About Clients' Money]

19
01:00.233 --> 01:02.989
[Pure Evil: Target Kitchen Sakoda Destroyed!]

20
01:02.989 --> 01:04.881
These awful people!

21
01:04.881 --> 01:08.481
She probably felt that this scandal was hurting Tuesla's revival,

22
01:08.481 --> 01:11.069
and so that's why she left.

23
01:12.701 --> 01:15.745
I'll tell her not to pay any attention to that kind of stuff!

24
01:15.745 --> 01:18.705
Hold on a second!

25
01:18.705 --> 01:22.433
Don't you realize why Ms. Kusakabe went so far

26
01:22.433 --> 01:24.656
as to make you hate her with those harsh words?

27
01:24.656 --> 01:26.525
I know why.

28
01:26.525 --> 01:27.905
I'm not telling you, though.

29
01:27.905 --> 01:30.889
Because you'd try to drag her back like this!

30
01:30.889 --> 01:33.061
That won't change anything.

31
01:33.061 --> 01:38.033
Unless we ease Ms. Kusakabe's anxiety, she won't come back.

32
01:40.881 --> 01:43.117
- Then what should I do? - Until the scandal blows over,

33
01:43.117 --> 01:45.525
keep Tuesla's spark alive.

34
01:45.525 --> 01:50.929
Build up Tuesla so much that Ms. Kusakabe feels safe coming back.

35
01:51.553 --> 01:53.045
And then...

36
01:53.045 --> 01:55.185
Marriage?

37
01:55.185 --> 01:57.601
- I don't know about that, but... - I see.

38
01:57.601 --> 01:59.233
All right!

39
01:59.233 --> 02:02.541
Just wait, O-Con!

40
02:02.541 --> 02:04.670
[Super! Good Mood Festival!] ♪ Spring, Magic, Magic ♪

41
02:04.670 --> 02:07.249
♪ Stand up! Love and bow! Yeah! ♪

42
02:07.249 --> 02:10.641
♪ Three, two, one. Spring, Magic, Magic ♪

43
02:10.641 --> 02:12.781
Try some Zapaan!

44
02:12.781 --> 02:16.621
One sip will wash your troubles away! How about some Zapaan?

45
02:16.621 --> 02:19.885
- Thank you very much. - Thank you!

46
02:19.885 --> 02:21.461
Nice!

47
02:21.461 --> 02:24.721
Your smile is so gentle, Ms. Kusakabe!

48
02:24.721 --> 02:26.333
In comparison...

49
02:26.333 --> 02:27.669
This is Zapaan.

50
02:27.669 --> 02:30.521
- It'll improve your gut health... - Hey, you!

51
02:30.521 --> 02:32.233
- You're way too stiff! - Ah, wait...

52
02:32.233 --> 02:34.109
Your smile is as hard as a baguette!

53
02:34.109 --> 02:36.269
- Sorry. - Soften it up!

54
02:36.269 --> 02:38.121
- Yes. - Go on!

55
02:38.825 --> 02:40.121
This is Japan! Uh...

56
02:40.121 --> 02:41.481
- This is Zapaan. - What are you saying?

57
02:41.481 --> 02:43.205
- The power of lactic acid... - More, more!

58
02:43.205 --> 02:44.866
- Swirl it all around! - Go on! Zapaan!

59
02:44.866 --> 02:48.900
Ever since I closed the restaurant, I've had nothing to do.

60
02:48.900 --> 02:50.621
So I took a part-time job.

61
02:50.621 --> 02:51.745
Oh?

62
02:51.745 --> 02:54.165
You're not reopening the restaurant?

63
02:54.165 --> 02:56.677
Why not run it together with your former wife as exes?

64
02:57.821 --> 02:59.589
[Learn Rosy Investment Tips] She's no longer

65
02:59.589 --> 03:01.065
[from Ms. Sakoda] the wife I knew.

66
03:01.065 --> 03:03.153
[Challengers Winning in the Accelerating Business World]

67
03:03.153 --> 03:05.893
You didn't have to quit your job, though.

68
03:05.893 --> 03:07.345
Well...

69
03:07.345 --> 03:08.481
A lot happened.

70
03:08.481 --> 03:10.509
Because of the scandal, right?

71
03:10.509 --> 03:12.917
Go back once it blows over, okay?

72
03:12.917 --> 03:14.641
Seriously.

73
03:17.193 --> 03:20.545
What should we do to stage Tuesla's big comeback?

74
03:20.545 --> 03:23.885
Create some friends for Tuesla.

75
03:23.885 --> 03:24.961
Friends?

76
03:24.961 --> 03:27.200
Like Mimmy for Hello Kitty,

77
03:27.200 --> 03:30.433
or Nonnon for Sunsun.

78
03:40.521 --> 03:43.541
- Hello, this is Omishima Design. - Seo Design!

79
03:45.337 --> 03:47.741
How's the sales trip going?

80
03:47.741 --> 03:51.989
Well, I visited shops all over Tokyo,

81
03:51.989 --> 03:55.613
but due to the scandal, I haven't really gotten any good responses.

82
03:55.613 --> 03:56.697
Tokyo?

83
03:56.697 --> 04:00.025
Aren't you misunderstanding something, Mr. Hirose?

84
04:00.025 --> 04:01.121
What do you mean?

85
04:01.121 --> 04:04.037
I didn't want you to go around Tokyo,

86
04:04.037 --> 04:09.389
but to our cash cow nation that's full of Mizuki Seo fans.

87
04:09.389 --> 04:11.533
The Republic of Tektorian.

88
04:11.533 --> 04:13.900
I'm on my way!

89
04:15.066 --> 04:19.057
Ms. Sasaoka, you're good at taking candid sneaky photos, right?

90
04:19.057 --> 04:22.833
No, no, I wouldn't say I'm good at it.

91
04:31.366 --> 04:32.513
Like this?

92
04:32.513 --> 04:34.193
Oh, yeah, yeah.

93
04:34.193 --> 04:35.285
Okay, Mr. Seo,

94
04:35.285 --> 04:38.937
now gently place your hand on Mr. Omishima's back.

95
04:38.937 --> 04:41.121
- Gently? - Yes.

96
04:42.021 --> 04:44.089
Gently. Good, good.

97
04:44.089 --> 04:47.477
Ah, don't look at the camera. It ruins the look of a candid, sneaky photo.

98
04:47.477 --> 04:48.929
Keep it natural.

99
04:48.929 --> 04:51.481
Now sit next to him and put an arm around his shoulder.

100
04:51.481 --> 04:54.069
Great. Yes, very good. Thank you.

101
04:54.069 --> 04:57.393
Okay, Mr. Omishima, now please do that fake cry that's your specialty.

102
04:57.393 --> 05:00.341
Nice. You're crying. You're crying.

103
05:00.341 --> 05:03.517
Yes, now look like you're full of regret. Deep regret.

104
05:03.517 --> 05:06.777
- I regret everything. - Ah, you're even saying it!

105
05:06.777 --> 05:10.193
Even though it's a photo, that remorse really comes through.

106
05:10.193 --> 05:13.521
A touching untold story: Mizuki Seo reaches out

107
05:13.521 --> 05:17.089
to save washed-up loser Omishima.

108
05:17.089 --> 05:19.553
Using my twenty burner accounts,

109
05:19.553 --> 05:21.893
- I'll hype up this story. - Twenty?

110
05:21.893 --> 05:24.733
The tide will turn.

111
05:24.733 --> 05:25.733
[The handsome Mizuki Seo saves the scandalous Mr. Omishima]

112
05:25.733 --> 05:26.817
[So heartwarming! Check out this article!]

113
05:26.817 --> 05:28.645
[Wow, Mr. Seo is so sweet!] Amazing.

114
05:33.069 --> 05:36.137
- One, please. - Thank you very much.

115
05:36.137 --> 05:38.433
Oh, Mr. Fuchinobe! What are you doing here?

116
05:38.433 --> 05:40.893
I heard from Ms. Kominami.

117
05:40.893 --> 05:42.585
She said that you quit Seo Design,

118
05:42.585 --> 05:45.705
but you seem lingeringly attached. [*Pun on "back-hair pulled" in Japanese]

119
05:45.705 --> 05:48.801
I'm not lingering at all. My hair is silky smooth.

120
05:48.801 --> 05:52.637
So I wanted to help you out,

121
05:52.637 --> 05:55.137
and I went to gather some info on Seo Design.

122
05:57.765 --> 05:58.768
Amazing.

123
05:58.768 --> 06:01.269
- Full of regret. - This is a glimpse of

124
06:01.269 --> 06:03.769
- You're even saying it! - the Mizuki Seo Image Boost Campaign.

125
06:03.769 --> 06:07.673
Thanks to this, the backlash is starting to die down.

126
06:07.673 --> 06:08.773
[Saving that trash Mr. Omishima? What a huge heart!]

127
06:08.773 --> 06:09.905
[He really is a prince!]

128
06:09.905 --> 06:10.981
[I always knew he was a good guy deep down!]

129
06:10.981 --> 06:12.025
[So now that shady consultant is gone, and Tuesla's back?]

130
06:12.025 --> 06:13.781
[Everyone flipped opinions, but leaving that consultant was the right move]

131
06:14.909 --> 06:18.037
[Turns out he's actually a good guy] What's with this pose?

132
06:18.037 --> 06:19.765
Is it trending?

133
06:24.873 --> 06:27.669
Just you wait, O-Con!

134
06:27.669 --> 06:29.761
O-Con?

135
06:29.761 --> 06:32.085
[O-Con]

136
06:35.853 --> 06:37.805
He's coming.

137
06:37.805 --> 06:40.400
Once Tuesla makes a comeback, he'll definitely...

138
06:41.617 --> 06:43.417
come.

139
06:44.777 --> 06:46.665
I have to move.

140
06:46.665 --> 06:48.837
I have to move before he comes.

141
06:48.837 --> 06:50.921
Oh! Ms. Kusakabe?

142
06:50.921 --> 06:55.609
- No, no, no! - Is Kitchen Sakoda doing well?

143
06:58.485 --> 07:00.382
- Ms. Kumi. - You've been visiting

144
07:00.382 --> 07:02.517
the main restaurant, right?

145
07:02.517 --> 07:06.281
It must be tough over there, but it's tough here too.

146
07:06.281 --> 07:11.069
Talking about our divorce on TV like that.

147
07:11.069 --> 07:14.333
Because of that, my company got dragged into a scandal too.

148
07:14.333 --> 07:16.600
Our sales plummeted.

149
07:17.941 --> 07:19.237
I'm so sorry.

150
07:19.237 --> 07:21.473
Are you going to take responsibility?

151
07:22.453 --> 07:23.469
Responsibility?

152
07:23.469 --> 07:25.366
Come on. Let's go.

153
07:27.085 --> 07:28.821
Mr. Taira,

154
07:28.821 --> 07:32.777
this woman was introduced by our outside director, Ms. Kumi Sakoda,

155
07:32.777 --> 07:36.361
and has been appointed as a consultant for Merry.

156
07:36.361 --> 07:38.573
Her name is Anna Kusakabe.

157
07:41.029 --> 07:44.566
Do your best. Just like you did for us.

158
07:57.721 --> 07:59.665
[Final Episode]

159
07:59.665 --> 08:01.833
I'm very sorry.

160
08:01.833 --> 08:05.029
Swept along by Ms. Kumi's momentum, I ended up coming here,

161
08:05.029 --> 08:08.509
[Wash your hands and gargle] but me consulting for Merry is a bit...

162
08:08.509 --> 08:10.645
So regarding this matter...

163
08:11.249 --> 08:12.965
All right!

164
08:12.965 --> 08:15.837
- Ms. Kusakabe! Well... - Oh, my God!

165
08:15.837 --> 08:19.361
My comment caused so much trouble.

166
08:19.361 --> 08:22.761
I am really, truly sorry!

167
08:22.761 --> 08:26.497
Well... Rena, you don't need to apologize.

168
08:26.497 --> 08:29.113
- Well then... - Actually,

169
08:29.113 --> 08:32.253
ever since then, our sales have been terrible.

170
08:32.253 --> 08:35.857
I thought our numbers would recover if the president changed,

171
08:35.857 --> 08:38.579
but the new president basically just goes

172
08:38.579 --> 08:42.917
"Mmm..." all the time.

173
08:42.917 --> 08:46.873
- Listen, I really... - Please, I beg you!

174
08:46.873 --> 08:49.449
Please save Merry.

175
08:49.449 --> 08:53.333
Well...

176
08:55.053 --> 08:58.889
We've already started restructuring staff

177
08:58.889 --> 09:01.797
and asking for voluntary resignations.

178
09:01.797 --> 09:06.093
If this keeps up, we'll be looking at bankruptcy.

179
09:07.709 --> 09:11.817
By the way, if it comes to that, what will happen to the characters?

180
09:11.817 --> 09:16.285
They'll likely all be sold off before bankruptcy.

181
09:16.285 --> 09:19.245
Berry might sell,

182
09:19.245 --> 09:23.313
but the other characters have almost no name recognition,

183
09:23.313 --> 09:26.277
so I don't know if anyone will buy them.

184
09:26.277 --> 09:28.713
And the same goes for Cynical Molco.

185
09:28.713 --> 09:31.766
With the bad reputation from the scandal,

186
09:31.766 --> 09:34.949
even lowering the price might not help.

187
09:34.949 --> 09:39.117
And any unsold characters will never again...

188
09:39.117 --> 09:42.009
[Full Tummy Molco]

189
09:49.117 --> 09:54.766
Even if they're not famous, or have a tainted image,

190
09:55.725 --> 09:58.133
there are still people who love them.

191
10:00.505 --> 10:04.217
There definitely are!

192
10:04.217 --> 10:09.161
And making people like those sad is something that must never happen!

193
10:09.161 --> 10:11.433
Ms. Kusakabe...

194
10:11.433 --> 10:14.753
Let's do it! Let's revive Merry!

195
10:14.753 --> 10:19.866
For the characters, and for the people who love them!

196
10:20.721 --> 10:25.441
[One Month Later]

197
10:35.601 --> 10:39.289
The tie-up contract for Tuesla is signed!

198
10:40.809 --> 10:43.245
[All Japan Heavy Industries, Tie-up Commercial Proposal]

199
10:43.245 --> 10:45.885
A commercial at last.

200
10:45.885 --> 10:47.493
Iron Tuesla looks great.

201
10:47.493 --> 10:50.045
We finally made it this far after that scandal.

202
10:50.045 --> 10:51.937
You're in the way.

203
10:51.937 --> 10:53.797
What? A trip? Trip-mishima?

204
10:53.797 --> 10:57.133
Explain it to him, Ms. Sasaoka. I'm busy.

205
10:57.133 --> 10:59.785
- He's going to Tektorian. - Tektorian?

206
10:59.785 --> 11:03.661
There's a festival coming up soon, celebrating their World Heritage fortress.

207
11:03.661 --> 11:06.266
It's called the Tektorian Castle Hustle Carnival.

208
11:06.266 --> 11:07.633
He's going to attend that.

209
11:07.633 --> 11:09.993
Sightseeing, then! Giddy-mishima!

210
11:09.993 --> 11:12.845
Not at all! It's Work-mishima!

211
11:12.845 --> 11:16.757
One million tourists from around the world attend this festival,

212
11:16.757 --> 11:18.489
and everyone gets hyped up.

213
11:18.489 --> 11:21.713
And at a festival like that...

214
11:21.713 --> 11:24.817
Wow, it's Tuesla! Castle Tuesla!

215
11:24.817 --> 11:26.889
Thanks to Mr. Hirose's PR efforts,

216
11:26.889 --> 11:28.965
as a new character created by the same designer

217
11:28.965 --> 11:31.245
who came up with Cho-cho-cho-cho-cho-cho-cho, Tuesla is really popular.

218
11:31.245 --> 11:35.053
Despite having all the right conditions in place to expand recognition,

219
11:35.053 --> 11:37.865
Mr. Hirose still can't speak a word of Tektorian.

220
11:37.865 --> 11:39.557
So I am...

221
11:39.557 --> 11:41.393
Wait, you speak it?

222
11:41.393 --> 11:44.745
[*Speaking Tektorian]

223
11:45.857 --> 11:48.329
- What did you say? - I'll leave the rest to you.

224
11:48.329 --> 11:51.013
I'll be counting on you.

225
11:51.013 --> 11:54.533
- Well... - I was talking to Mr. Shiiba.

226
11:55.677 --> 11:57.513
Leave it to me.

227
11:57.513 --> 11:59.297
Well, then.

228
11:59.297 --> 12:01.166
Bring back some souvenirs.

229
12:09.297 --> 12:10.309
Man,

230
12:10.309 --> 12:12.341
[Seo Design New Character] Tuesla is really taking off.

231
12:12.341 --> 12:13.733
[Tutu-Tuesla] Indeed.

232
12:13.733 --> 12:16.769
[Saying that a consultant] Plus, Ms. Kusakabe's scandal,

233
12:16.769 --> 12:18.585
[caused my divorce] ever since Ms. Kumi's post,

234
12:18.585 --> 12:20.713
[is an unacceptable accusation] has pretty much cooled down.

235
12:32.865 --> 12:35.266
I think now's your chance.

236
12:42.065 --> 12:45.133
Just wait, O-Con!

237
12:50.237 --> 12:53.161
Hello, this is Sasaoka from Seo Design.

238
12:54.833 --> 12:56.721
What?

239
12:58.557 --> 13:00.193
It's from Merry.

240
13:00.193 --> 13:01.965
What?

241
13:18.109 --> 13:19.785
So about today's meeting...

242
13:19.785 --> 13:22.997
They want to discuss Molco's future development

243
13:22.997 --> 13:26.329
with you as the creator.

244
13:26.329 --> 13:28.097
Oh.

245
13:28.825 --> 13:31.689
- What kind of discussion? - As I said, details are...

246
13:31.689 --> 13:33.913
Thank you for waiting.

247
13:33.913 --> 13:37.505
Thank you for making time to meet with us today.

248
13:38.125 --> 13:42.653
This is our president and CEO, Mr. Taira.

249
13:42.653 --> 13:44.697
Nice to meet you.

250
13:46.305 --> 13:48.033
In addition,

251
13:49.429 --> 13:51.393
the person handling this project,

252
13:51.393 --> 13:55.629
our consultant, Ms. Kusakabe, will also be joining us.

253
13:55.629 --> 13:57.473
It's been a while.

254
14:01.913 --> 14:03.325
[Planning and Development Meeting] Our company has decided

255
14:03.325 --> 14:07.309
to produce a new Cynical Molco movie.

256
14:07.309 --> 14:12.733
We hope to make it a sequel that builds on the previous momentum.

257
14:12.733 --> 14:16.709
We have decided to have dual leads.

258
14:16.709 --> 14:19.393
One, of course, is Cynical Molco.

259
14:19.393 --> 14:21.281
And the other is this one.

260
14:22.333 --> 14:24.089
Full Tummy Molco.

261
14:24.089 --> 14:26.129
In this film, Full Tummy Molco

262
14:26.129 --> 14:30.313
will appear as Cynical Molco's twin sister.

263
14:30.313 --> 14:32.113
[Dual Leads] And for this film's director,

264
14:32.113 --> 14:35.769
we've brought in world-renowned Ryo Fukami,

265
14:35.769 --> 14:37.937
- with the screenplay by Yuiko Ninomaru... - Well, excuse me...

266
14:37.937 --> 14:39.737
Well...

267
14:39.737 --> 14:41.137
Personally,

268
14:41.137 --> 14:46.869
I'm very glad to see Full Tummy Molco finally see the light of day.

269
14:46.869 --> 14:49.221
But why so suddenly?

270
14:49.221 --> 14:53.217
Out of respect for you as the designer, Mr. Seo,

271
14:53.217 --> 14:57.713
we reached out, hoping to get your input in a supervisory role.

272
14:57.713 --> 14:59.509
Supervisor?

273
15:02.181 --> 15:05.166
Well... Mr. Seo?

274
15:06.557 --> 15:09.166
Mr. Seo. Mr. Seo.

275
15:09.829 --> 15:11.705
I get it!

276
15:11.705 --> 15:14.169
Revenge. That's it.

277
15:14.169 --> 15:17.245
You want to get back at Merry for dragging Tuesla into a scandal

278
15:17.245 --> 15:19.049
- by destroying them from within... - No.

279
15:19.049 --> 15:20.877
Wait, that's not it?

280
15:22.833 --> 15:24.673
Now I get it!

281
15:24.673 --> 15:26.900
Rehab. That's it.

282
15:26.900 --> 15:29.417
You took a break from consulting, so this is a warm-up

283
15:29.417 --> 15:31.133
- before coming back to us... - No.

284
15:31.133 --> 15:33.300
I just accepted a normal client request. That's all.

285
15:33.300 --> 15:36.861
- Then what if we also hire you normally... - Not possible.

286
15:36.861 --> 15:38.821
Huh? What?

287
15:38.821 --> 15:40.389
Mr. Seo. Mr. Seo?

288
15:40.389 --> 15:43.169
- Mr. Seo! - You ditched us and quit,

289
15:43.169 --> 15:44.845
so why are you working at Merry like nothing happened?

290
15:44.845 --> 15:46.765
It makes no sense! Am I wrong?

291
15:46.765 --> 15:49.467
- We're not talking about that... - Yes, we are!

292
15:49.467 --> 15:51.685
What, you're a Merry person now?

293
15:51.685 --> 15:53.537
Has your brain gone all Merry too?

294
15:53.537 --> 15:55.733
You don't care about Tuesla at all, do you?

295
15:56.565 --> 16:00.105
We worked and worked and worked

296
16:00.105 --> 16:02.425
so you could feel safe coming back to us!

297
16:02.425 --> 16:04.801
And yet you betray us so casually!

298
16:04.801 --> 16:06.977
In the end,

299
16:06.977 --> 16:10.693
you never cared about Tuesla or Seo Design!

300
16:11.445 --> 16:13.265
- You're just totally half-hearted! - I already told you

301
16:13.265 --> 16:15.133
why I quit Seo Design.

302
16:15.133 --> 16:17.181
Shall I say it again?

303
16:17.181 --> 16:21.549
Word for word, the exact reason I gave that day.

304
16:21.549 --> 16:23.257
- Shall I repeat it right here? - Well...

305
16:23.257 --> 16:25.061
Ms. Kusakabe?

306
16:28.757 --> 16:30.685
Do whatever you want.

307
16:31.749 --> 16:33.321
Not that I approve.

308
16:33.321 --> 16:34.501
Thank you.

309
16:34.501 --> 16:38.200
Moving forward, we will proceed based on our own judgment.

310
16:40.765 --> 16:42.549
That's all.

311
16:59.365 --> 17:01.666
Excuse us. Excuse us.

312
17:08.465 --> 17:10.213
How is Mr. Seo doing?

313
17:11.229 --> 17:14.765
He's back to how he was the day Ms. Kusakabe left.

314
17:14.765 --> 17:17.305
Well, after being told that...

315
17:17.305 --> 17:20.637
Merry really is such a troublesome company.

316
17:20.637 --> 17:22.234
Well, you're the one who pushed them

317
17:22.234 --> 17:24.285
to the brink of bankruptcy, Mr. Omishima.

318
17:24.285 --> 17:26.489
So, how are things over there?

319
17:26.489 --> 17:29.745
Oh, it's amazing.

320
17:29.745 --> 17:32.266
The whole country is gearing up for the Castle Hustle Carnival,

321
17:32.266 --> 17:34.673
and everyone here is ready to hustle!

322
17:34.673 --> 17:37.437
We can expect even higher profits than anticipated.

323
17:37.437 --> 17:38.593
Impressive as always.

324
17:38.593 --> 17:42.105
Hey, why not bring Mr. Seo over here too?

325
17:42.105 --> 17:43.845
It'll cheer him up.

326
17:43.845 --> 17:48.541
Everyone's chanting, "Seo! Seo!"

327
18:13.289 --> 18:15.121
Mugi!

328
18:21.113 --> 18:22.677
I see.

329
18:22.677 --> 18:26.945
So you're just trying to protect Full Tummy Molco.

330
18:27.677 --> 18:33.089
Of course. I'm doing all this on my own, and he doesn't know.

331
18:33.089 --> 18:35.800
Still, saying it like that...

332
18:37.889 --> 18:39.629
Anna,

333
18:40.301 --> 18:43.549
you really love Mr. Seo, don't you?

334
18:44.441 --> 18:46.617
Yeah.

335
18:46.617 --> 18:49.733
I think I do.

336
18:52.505 --> 18:53.877
I see.

337
18:53.877 --> 18:55.201
Sorry, I lied.

338
18:55.201 --> 18:57.077
Huh?

339
18:58.497 --> 19:01.545
I love him. I love him so much!

340
19:01.545 --> 19:03.709
Ah, okay.

341
19:03.709 --> 19:06.957
Even I myself don't really know why,

342
19:06.957 --> 19:09.937
but when I heard his war cry at the proposal pitch,

343
19:09.937 --> 19:15.193
and when I heard that he'd turned down the ambassador role, my heart fluttered.

344
19:15.193 --> 19:19.001
I told myself that for Tuesla's sake, I couldn't fall for him,

345
19:19.001 --> 19:22.969
but seeing him and arguing with him today,

346
19:22.969 --> 19:27.133
all I could think was, "I love him!"

347
19:28.901 --> 19:32.713
Right now, if something were to happen,

348
19:32.713 --> 19:35.701
I'd probably put Mr. Seo first,

349
19:35.701 --> 19:38.266
even if it meant sacrificing Tuesla.

350
19:39.537 --> 19:45.201
And Mr. Seo would probably do the same.

351
19:45.201 --> 19:47.200
Is that...

352
19:51.473 --> 19:53.209
Is that a bad thing?

353
19:53.209 --> 19:57.701
We're the ones who created Tuesla to share with everyone,

354
19:57.701 --> 20:00.261
so we should prioritize Tuesla above all else.

355
20:00.261 --> 20:02.189
We have that responsibility.

356
20:02.189 --> 20:06.737
Letting our feelings cloud that judgment

357
20:07.805 --> 20:10.289
is irresponsible,

358
20:10.289 --> 20:12.249
because we are its creators.

359
20:13.533 --> 20:17.100
Why don't you tell that to Mr. Seo?

360
20:22.369 --> 20:26.300
For everyone's sake...

361
20:27.409 --> 20:30.033
Is love really such a bad thing?

362
20:31.185 --> 20:34.765
I think your love

363
20:34.765 --> 20:37.817
and the love from the person who taught you how to love

364
20:37.817 --> 20:39.749
are both wonderful.

365
20:53.800 --> 20:56.453
You can't handle alcohol.

366
20:56.453 --> 20:58.905
The last one, number 100!

367
21:02.297 --> 21:05.529
[Can't Stop Pasta Snack]

368
21:07.081 --> 21:08.945
Excuse me, could you ring these up?

369
21:08.945 --> 21:11.393
- Welcome... Huh? - Huh?

370
21:11.393 --> 21:14.681
Ah, are you working a gap part-time job?

371
21:15.757 --> 21:17.413
I see.

372
21:17.413 --> 21:19.429
[Can't Stop Pasta Snack]

373
21:19.429 --> 21:21.709
- Ah... - No, no.

374
21:25.109 --> 21:29.766
Actually, Kumi came to the shop...

375
21:36.041 --> 21:37.853
There you are.

376
21:39.541 --> 21:41.893
I'll go grab some bags.

377
21:41.893 --> 21:44.893
Oh, no, I...

378
21:57.557 --> 21:59.437
I'm sorry.

379
22:01.657 --> 22:02.853
No...

380
22:02.853 --> 22:07.189
I was the one getting emotional and saying rude things during work...

381
22:07.189 --> 22:08.781
Not for that.

382
22:08.781 --> 22:10.677
I'm saying sorry for...

383
22:13.693 --> 22:15.577
I'm sorry for falling in love with you.

384
22:17.421 --> 22:22.866
My love pulled you away from the things you love.

385
22:25.633 --> 22:26.989
- Well... - I mean,

386
22:26.989 --> 22:29.081
you love Tuesla so much.

387
22:29.893 --> 22:33.349
You still love and rely on it so much.

388
22:33.349 --> 22:39.133
Yet I confessed my feelings and made you quit your job.

389
22:41.593 --> 22:43.381
I'm sorry.

390
22:46.605 --> 22:48.385
I won't say it anymore.

391
22:49.125 --> 22:51.941
I'll never talk about love or marriage again.

392
22:51.941 --> 22:54.025
In fact, I'll forget it.

393
22:54.025 --> 22:55.861
I'll act like none of it happened.

394
22:57.113 --> 22:59.809
So that's why we can do this.

395
22:59.809 --> 23:03.073
- I can supervise the movie. - Huh?

396
23:03.073 --> 23:07.501
I know you care deeply about Full Tummy Molco,

397
23:08.233 --> 23:10.673
and Molco is my responsibility.

398
23:10.673 --> 23:14.133
Besides, honestly, that premise was boring.

399
23:14.133 --> 23:17.833
- Boring... - So business is business.

400
23:17.833 --> 23:21.589
Let's leave feelings out of it.

401
23:21.589 --> 23:23.713
In short...

402
23:23.713 --> 23:25.766
I look forward to working with you.

403
23:33.393 --> 23:36.233
Yes, likewise.

404
23:36.233 --> 23:38.509
I look forward to working with you.

405
23:38.509 --> 23:41.809
- So we have a deal? - Yes.

406
23:41.809 --> 23:44.433
- Let's sign. - Sign...

407
23:56.021 --> 23:58.121
Yeah.

408
23:58.121 --> 24:00.541
No tingling spark when we touch anymore.

409
24:08.493 --> 24:11.381
See you.

410
24:11.381 --> 24:13.249
Okay.

411
24:18.657 --> 24:22.133
It's tingling...

412
24:27.437 --> 24:29.761
[So love doesn't need a correct answer]

413
24:31.361 --> 24:32.453
- How is it? - Well,

414
24:32.453 --> 24:35.297
- it's boring. - Boring... What?

415
24:35.297 --> 24:38.457
You told me to give honest feedback.

416
24:38.457 --> 24:41.245
Still, as a consultant, shouldn't you sugarcoat it

417
24:41.245 --> 24:43.266
to motivate the other person?

418
24:43.266 --> 24:45.329
Then do you really think this premise

419
24:45.329 --> 24:47.593
for Cynical Molco and Full Tummy Molco isn't boring?

420
24:48.581 --> 24:50.713
But compared to the one you came up with the other day,

421
24:50.713 --> 24:52.829
it's not exactly not-not-boring.

422
24:52.829 --> 24:54.329
- Not not-not-boring. - Huh?

423
24:54.329 --> 24:57.297
Mine's more not-boring...

424
24:57.297 --> 24:58.829
Too many 'nots.' And you stumbled.

425
24:58.829 --> 25:02.009
- Twelve... - One more time.

426
25:02.009 --> 25:03.721
This way.

427
25:05.105 --> 25:08.301
Can this place not even afford security guards?

428
25:08.301 --> 25:10.333
Any suspicious person can just waltz in.

429
25:10.333 --> 25:12.805
Aren't you supposed to be in Tektorian?

430
25:12.805 --> 25:15.998
Actually, a huge crisis has occurred in Tektorian.

431
25:15.998 --> 25:19.577
- Mr. Shiiba, hurry and get ready. - Yes, sir.

432
25:19.577 --> 25:22.133
Wait, what's going on?

433
25:28.277 --> 25:30.621
I'm so glad you're safe.

434
25:30.621 --> 25:31.725
Yeah.

435
25:31.725 --> 25:33.885
Wait, Ms. Kusakabe?

436
25:33.885 --> 25:35.066
Where are you right now?

437
25:35.066 --> 25:38.169
Well, they said there was an accident...

438
25:38.169 --> 25:41.733
The fortress suddenly collapsed.

439
25:43.349 --> 25:44.945
Can you see? Well...

440
25:44.945 --> 25:48.389
It looked like it could crumble at any moment anyway,

441
25:48.389 --> 25:51.553
but the people of Tektorian are so laid-back.

442
25:51.553 --> 25:53.549
And well, being that way,

443
25:53.549 --> 25:57.081
safety measures fell behind, and this happened.

444
25:57.081 --> 25:59.485
Then what about the Castle Hustle Carnival?

445
25:59.485 --> 26:01.700
It's canceled, of course.

446
26:02.693 --> 26:05.985
The locals were really looking forward to it,

447
26:05.985 --> 26:09.461
so everyone is in shock, and the whole country feels gloomy.

448
26:09.461 --> 26:12.221
As for the Tuesla shipments that we'd planned for them,

449
26:12.221 --> 26:14.933
they won't be in the mood to buy luxury goods for a while,

450
26:14.933 --> 26:16.965
so please cancel all orders.

451
26:16.965 --> 26:18.689
Understood.

452
26:20.925 --> 26:22.641
What are you doing?

453
26:23.321 --> 26:26.733
We're sending plushies. For free.

454
26:26.733 --> 26:28.433
What do you mean, for free?

455
26:28.433 --> 26:30.229
There are people there

456
26:30.889 --> 26:35.861
who love Seo Design's characters and were looking forward to them.

457
26:35.861 --> 26:38.325
Right now, those people are feeling down.

458
26:38.325 --> 26:39.565
That's exactly when they need Tuesla!

459
26:39.565 --> 26:41.705
Is that really what they need?

460
26:42.349 --> 26:45.981
What they need right now is repair funds,

461
26:45.981 --> 26:49.021
heavy machinery, and manpower, isn't it?

462
26:49.021 --> 26:50.913
That may be true, but...

463
26:57.613 --> 26:59.433
Let's send them.

464
27:02.501 --> 27:04.549
Ah, sorry, I'm an outsider, but...

465
27:04.549 --> 27:06.369
Go on.

466
27:07.225 --> 27:11.113
Of course, money is extremely important.

467
27:11.113 --> 27:15.057
However, when you're about to give up,

468
27:15.693 --> 27:21.493
the things that support you can be many things besides money, right?

469
27:21.493 --> 27:27.005
Like sports, songs, favorite idols, characters,

470
27:27.005 --> 27:30.613
or support from strangers whom you've never met.

471
27:31.257 --> 27:37.001
And right now, Seo Design can send Tuesla.

472
27:37.001 --> 27:40.789
You can send Tuesla to people who are hurting.

473
27:40.789 --> 27:42.881
So shouldn't you do it?

474
27:42.881 --> 27:48.005
I'm sure Tuesla will give them strength.

475
27:48.901 --> 27:51.473
All right, let's do it!

476
27:51.473 --> 27:54.177
- Send all our stock to Tektorian! - That's 500 plushies.

477
27:54.177 --> 27:56.261
Only 500? We can do more!

478
27:56.261 --> 27:58.765
- But... - Sending more than that for free

479
27:58.765 --> 28:01.461
will harm Seo Design's operations.

480
28:01.461 --> 28:05.357
Five hundred is our absolute limit.

481
28:05.357 --> 28:08.329
No, that's nowhere near enough...

482
28:11.065 --> 28:13.600
Well... What is it?

483
28:16.933 --> 28:21.265
Can Merry help with that too?

484
28:23.066 --> 28:25.645
Can Merry help with that too?

485
28:25.645 --> 28:29.393
He actually spoke. Twice, even.

486
28:30.349 --> 28:33.166
Still, we don't have that kind of budget.

487
28:33.166 --> 28:36.466
We may lack budget, but we still have inventory.

488
28:37.133 --> 28:42.609
So rather than having our characters sleep in a warehouse...

489
28:42.609 --> 28:44.041
That's cool.

490
28:44.041 --> 28:45.809
But even so,

491
28:45.809 --> 28:49.161
that won't be enough to reach all of Tektorian.

492
28:56.281 --> 29:00.233
Then why don't we get more companies like this?

493
29:00.233 --> 29:01.409
Like this?

494
29:01.409 --> 29:04.057
There's a limit to what we can do alone,

495
29:04.057 --> 29:08.341
but if more companies like Merry pitch in, we can make it happen.

496
29:08.341 --> 29:09.981
We can send plushies to all of Tektorian!

497
29:09.981 --> 29:11.721
But how?

498
29:11.721 --> 29:13.945
We just have to ask them!

499
29:13.945 --> 29:16.717
Ask them to send characters together and support Tektorian!

500
29:16.717 --> 29:18.649
Every single character company out there!

501
29:18.649 --> 29:22.125
Wait, you mean asking other companies?

502
29:22.125 --> 29:24.533
Is that a bad thing? Why not?

503
29:24.533 --> 29:27.966
No, I think it's wonderful.

504
29:28.793 --> 29:32.133
Let's do it. Let's reach out!

505
29:33.537 --> 29:37.533
All right, things are about to get busy!

506
29:40.301 --> 29:42.161
All right!

507
29:46.325 --> 29:47.485
[Sent] I just sent it.

508
29:47.485 --> 29:49.265
Print it out and hand it to everyone.

509
29:49.265 --> 29:51.433
Got it! Leave it to me!

510
29:52.977 --> 29:56.141
The news about the collapsed fortress in the Republic of Tektorian.

511
29:56.141 --> 29:57.589
Ah, have you heard about that?

512
29:57.589 --> 30:01.801
For the Republic of Tektorian, please lend us your support.

513
30:01.801 --> 30:04.233
Yes, thank you for your time.

514
30:14.337 --> 30:18.941
[Project Support The Republic of Tektorian] Chara Palette.

515
30:18.941 --> 30:22.909
How many discontinued plushies do you have left?

516
30:22.909 --> 30:25.633
We'd like to use them for relief aid in the Republic of Tektorian.

517
30:25.633 --> 30:29.361
Could you please donate plushies and cheering merchandise

518
30:29.361 --> 30:31.673
to the Republic of Tektorian?

519
30:33.117 --> 30:36.461
That's a pretty tough ask.

520
30:37.205 --> 30:39.169
Funassyi,

521
30:39.169 --> 30:41.545
before, when I came home feeling down in the dumps,

522
30:41.545 --> 30:43.097
I saw you on TV,

523
30:43.097 --> 30:45.857
and found myself smiling without even realizing it.

524
30:45.857 --> 30:49.809
And right now, Tektorian needs your power, Funassyi! Please!

525
30:49.809 --> 30:53.000
Won't you lend us a hand?

526
30:54.789 --> 30:56.501
All right!

527
30:56.501 --> 30:58.445
Let Funassyi help out too!

528
30:58.445 --> 30:59.509
Thank you so much!

529
30:59.509 --> 31:01.700
You can count on me!

530
31:06.577 --> 31:08.333
Where should this go?

531
31:13.405 --> 31:14.557
[Kazuo Nimura: Dear Ms. Kusakabe, this is Kazuo Nimura from Peace Plus]

532
31:14.557 --> 31:15.613
[Regarding the aid you inquired about earlier,]

533
31:15.613 --> 31:17.865
[could our private jet be of any assistance?]

534
31:17.865 --> 31:23.600
Mr. Nimura from Peace Plus just offered the use of his private jet!

535
31:26.021 --> 31:28.685
[Project Support The Republic of Tektorian]

536
31:30.053 --> 31:32.257
Wait! That label is way too crooked!

537
31:32.257 --> 31:33.973
It's not crooked at all! Where is it crooked?

538
31:33.973 --> 31:35.033
- It's so diagonal - Come on!

539
31:35.033 --> 31:36.157
- you can't even read the letters! - Stop it, you two!

540
31:36.157 --> 31:38.009
- Cut it out. All right, all right. - Look, look!

541
31:38.009 --> 31:39.137
Snacks, snacks!

542
31:39.137 --> 31:41.725
- I brought you some snacks! - Thank you very much.

543
31:41.725 --> 31:43.433
That one's completely off too! Redo it!

544
31:43.433 --> 31:45.513
Honestly, Mr. Seo, you're obsessing over the labels

545
31:45.513 --> 31:46.557
- and barely making any - Aren't those two

546
31:46.557 --> 31:47.644
- progress at all! - dating?

547
31:47.644 --> 31:49.069
- Right? - I'm putting my heart into it!

548
31:49.069 --> 31:50.705
- Fine! We're through! - Apparently,

549
31:50.705 --> 31:52.361
- that's what they decided. - If we're through, then we're through!

550
31:52.361 --> 31:54.713
As long as it brings happiness to the people of Tektorian.

551
31:54.713 --> 31:55.845
It will!

552
31:55.845 --> 31:57.325
Because straight labels bring more joy!

553
31:57.325 --> 31:59.866
Way more joy than crooked ones do!

554
32:12.097 --> 32:17.017
[Always Together]

555
32:24.697 --> 32:26.217
Please take care of this.

556
32:26.217 --> 32:29.205
[Tektorian Castle Hustle Carnival, Cancelled]

557
33:01.929 --> 33:04.417
- Tuesla! - Tuesla!

558
33:04.417 --> 33:07.585
- Tuesla! - Tuesla!

559
33:07.585 --> 33:09.613
- Tuesla! - All right!

560
33:09.613 --> 33:11.589
- Tuesla! - Amazing!

561
33:11.589 --> 33:13.469
Tuesla!

562
33:13.469 --> 33:15.733
Tuesla!

563
33:47.681 --> 33:50.601
I was just thinking of heading out to get some breakfast.

564
33:50.601 --> 33:52.566
I was thinking the same thing.

565
33:54.013 --> 33:55.793
Well, then...

566
33:58.066 --> 34:01.033
- Ah, how about this? - Looks good.

567
34:07.285 --> 34:08.377
Welcome.

568
34:08.377 --> 34:10.781
Oh, you're working today too?

569
34:11.705 --> 34:14.566
Man, you sure eat a lot.

570
34:16.657 --> 34:18.849
[Can't Stop Pasta Snack]

571
34:21.897 --> 34:24.433
Excuse me, could you add this too?

572
34:27.313 --> 34:29.385
You know,

573
34:29.385 --> 34:34.269
ever since I was young, it was always cooking, cooking...

574
34:34.269 --> 34:37.577
Just focused on making delicious meals.

575
34:37.577 --> 34:39.300
But she...

576
34:40.277 --> 34:44.317
Ever since Kumi met you,

577
34:44.317 --> 34:47.969
she started talking about money all the time.

578
34:47.969 --> 34:52.297
And one day, she told me

579
34:52.949 --> 34:58.869
not to obsess so much over the restaurant and the flavor of its food.

580
34:58.869 --> 35:02.665
I thought, "It's over."

581
35:02.665 --> 35:08.977
I got stubborn, thinking that I had to protect the restaurant on my own.

582
35:08.977 --> 35:10.877
And then...

583
35:13.549 --> 35:15.629
I lost her,

584
35:15.629 --> 35:20.009
and in the end, I even lost the restaurant.

585
35:21.973 --> 35:26.233
[Can't Stop Pasta Snack] I wonder what I was even trying to protect.

586
35:31.685 --> 35:37.093
But then the other day, Kumi came by the restaurant.

587
35:37.093 --> 35:38.941
What?

588
35:39.697 --> 35:44.865
Before it closes, I wanted to come see it one last time.

589
35:46.617 --> 35:53.021
And she told me that just like me,

590
35:53.021 --> 35:59.266
she loved the restaurant, and she loved its food.

591
35:59.953 --> 36:02.257
I was stunned.

592
36:02.257 --> 36:05.521
Because she never gave any hint of that.

593
36:05.521 --> 36:11.213
In fact, she said the exact opposite.

594
36:21.637 --> 36:25.066
How people really feel

595
36:26.097 --> 36:31.397
isn't something you can easily figure out.

596
36:33.565 --> 36:36.673
Ah, sorry for rambling on about myself out of nowhere like that.

597
36:36.673 --> 36:38.413
Not at all.

598
36:45.341 --> 36:47.237
All right.

599
36:49.777 --> 36:53.577
[Project Support The Republic of Tektorian]

600
36:53.577 --> 36:57.745
[Led by Tuesla, Tektorian Relief Efforts Expand]

601
37:02.273 --> 37:03.969
Good morning.

602
37:03.969 --> 37:07.800
Look, Mr. Seo. Look at all these letters from Tektorian.

603
37:10.977 --> 37:16.733
I have no idea what they say, but I'm sure they're thrilled.

604
37:18.617 --> 37:21.033
Hey, O-Con,

605
37:21.033 --> 37:23.485
lately you've been here every single day, haven't you?

606
37:23.485 --> 37:26.966
Ah, yes, ever since setting up headquarters.

607
37:28.101 --> 37:31.813
Commuting feels like a waste of time,

608
37:31.813 --> 37:37.045
and I feel like there's a more efficient way.

609
37:37.737 --> 37:40.700
Wait, do you mean...

610
37:40.700 --> 37:43.566
Ah, well, I mean...

611
37:44.881 --> 37:46.700
Yes, exactly that.

612
37:48.769 --> 37:50.877
I'm so happy!

613
37:50.877 --> 37:53.353
So happy!

614
37:53.353 --> 37:55.085
Then marry...

615
37:58.721 --> 38:01.253
I've wanted this forever!

616
38:01.253 --> 38:04.366
Then I can glide around smoothly!

617
38:04.973 --> 38:07.833
You're a consultant, O-Con.

618
38:07.833 --> 38:11.666
Isn't a consultant's job to read people's feelings?

619
38:11.666 --> 38:13.973
Well, that's one aspect of it.

620
38:13.973 --> 38:16.733
But you have zero sense for that.

621
38:17.417 --> 38:19.533
Are you trying to irritate me again?

622
38:19.533 --> 38:23.921
Your misinterpretations are way worse than mine.

623
38:23.921 --> 38:25.200
No, they're not.

624
38:25.200 --> 38:27.169
Even if I am bad at interpreting things, at the very least,

625
38:27.169 --> 38:29.145
I'm definitely not worse than you.

626
38:29.145 --> 38:31.837
Oh, really? Is that so?

627
38:31.837 --> 38:35.697
I can read someone's feelings after just talking to them a little bit.

628
38:35.697 --> 38:37.221
Oh, is that so?

629
38:37.221 --> 38:38.645
Well, I don't even need words.

630
38:38.645 --> 38:41.745
Just by looking at their face, I know if they want to eat pineapple.

631
38:41.745 --> 38:44.229
Just from their face? Color me shocked.

632
38:44.229 --> 38:45.717
All right then, what about this face?

633
38:45.717 --> 38:47.933
What do you think I'm thinking? Go on.

634
38:48.833 --> 38:51.493
Yes, I've got it! You want to eat some Giant Cheap Bread Taro!

635
38:51.493 --> 38:55.033
Wrong! The correct answer was, "I want to get married."

636
38:56.657 --> 38:59.477
I won. I'm the real consultant.

637
38:59.477 --> 39:04.633
I'm Mizuki Seo-sultant...

638
39:07.857 --> 39:09.549
I'm sorry.

639
39:09.549 --> 39:12.353
No, wait. Talking to Mr. Sakoda earlier

640
39:12.353 --> 39:14.033
just made me feel kind of nostalgic.

641
39:14.033 --> 39:17.200
Anyway, my bad. I'm sorry.

642
39:19.569 --> 39:21.757
Huh?

643
39:21.757 --> 39:26.561
Huh? No, you calling yourself a consultant is what really shocks me.

644
39:26.561 --> 39:27.925
I said, I'm sorry.

645
39:27.925 --> 39:31.166
Then what about this face? What am I thinking right now?

646
39:33.117 --> 39:36.465
"How dare he talk about love and marriage again! I'm furious!"

647
39:36.465 --> 39:37.645
Wrong.

648
39:37.645 --> 39:39.533
It's my "I want to get married too" face.

649
39:39.533 --> 39:42.766
I win. I'm the consultant, the Kabe-sultant!

650
39:47.549 --> 39:49.766
And this is...

651
39:51.297 --> 39:54.200
my "but I'm still anxious" face.

652
39:56.413 --> 40:01.129
Your grandma once told me that love is so big

653
40:01.129 --> 40:05.200
that if you keep holding it, something will definitely spill over.

654
40:06.109 --> 40:08.433
That kind of scared me.

655
40:11.825 --> 40:14.000
But I still wanted to be with you.

656
40:15.345 --> 40:19.125
Yet being with you makes my love overflow,

657
40:19.125 --> 40:23.021
and just when I thought I couldn't handle it anymore,

658
40:23.021 --> 40:25.333
you told me you loved me.

659
40:28.417 --> 40:32.766
It might trouble you, and it might be selfish,

660
40:33.385 --> 40:35.177
but I'm going to say it.

661
40:38.237 --> 40:41.169
I love you, Mr. Seo.

662
40:54.829 --> 40:56.657
You know

663
40:57.861 --> 41:00.141
this is what Mizuki Seo said.

664
41:01.973 --> 41:04.183
Saying "I love you" to someone

665
41:04.853 --> 41:07.321
makes that person invincible.

666
41:09.321 --> 41:11.421
And just now,

667
41:11.421 --> 41:14.133
when you said that you love me, that's how I felt.

668
41:15.101 --> 41:17.105
Like there's nothing to be afraid of.

669
41:17.105 --> 41:19.245
Like I'm truly invincible.

670
41:20.597 --> 41:24.633
And because I'm invincible, I can do anything.

671
41:24.633 --> 41:29.545
And no matter how huge of a burden I hold, I won't let anything spill over.

672
41:29.545 --> 41:31.549
I'll carry it all.

673
41:31.549 --> 41:35.033
Love is amazing. Being invincible is amazing.

674
41:37.485 --> 41:41.709
So, I'm going to make you invincible too, O-Con.

675
41:43.585 --> 41:48.900
I love you...

676
41:55.045 --> 41:56.905
I love you.

677
41:57.573 --> 42:00.711
I love you, Mr. Seo!

678
42:00.711 --> 42:03.005
Hey...

679
42:05.621 --> 42:07.633
Yes! I win!

680
42:14.393 --> 42:17.617
I love you! I love you, O-Con!

681
42:17.617 --> 42:19.029
I love how you're almost always mad

682
42:19.029 --> 42:21.665
and how cute you are singing in the dark when you're down!

683
42:21.665 --> 42:23.533
I love everything! Alright, I win!

684
42:23.533 --> 42:27.461
What? Well, in that case, I love how much you love your grandma!

685
42:27.461 --> 42:29.333
And I love how pathetic and quick to cry you are!

686
42:29.333 --> 42:31.393
Love you, love you, love you, love you, love you!

687
42:31.393 --> 42:34.505
Love you! Love, love, love, love, love, love, love, love, love!

688
42:34.505 --> 42:36.180
- Ten loves! - Me too!

689
42:36.180 --> 42:39.745
Love, love, love, love, love, love, love, love, love, times 10 to the 10th.

690
42:39.745 --> 42:41.933
Times 10... I lose! Alright!

691
42:41.933 --> 42:44.513
- Love, love... Ten! - Ten... That's a tie.

692
42:44.513 --> 42:46.905
Do people really say "I love you" that much?

693
42:46.905 --> 42:50.405
- They've been keeping it bottled up. - Marriage! Marriage! Love!

694
42:52.545 --> 42:56.425
These are theatrical tears.

695
42:56.425 --> 43:00.021
- Go! Don't grab! - Love!

696
43:00.021 --> 43:02.781
- I said I love you! - Yes!

697
43:04.425 --> 43:07.521
- So cute! - I made friends!

698
43:07.521 --> 43:09.881
- So cute. - So cute.

699
43:09.881 --> 43:12.209
Super cute!

700
43:12.209 --> 43:14.605
- Cute. - So cute.

701
43:14.605 --> 43:16.229
Cute.

702
43:16.229 --> 43:18.800
- I love it. - I love it.

703
43:23.553 --> 43:26.413
So cute! I love this!

704
43:26.413 --> 43:28.545
- So cute. - I love it.

705
43:28.545 --> 43:30.581
Love it! I love this!

706
43:37.529 --> 43:39.401
I love it!

707
43:39.401 --> 43:41.593
How do you feel about being chosen as a new member?

708
43:41.593 --> 43:47.617
Well, I've been studying under the two of them all this time,

709
43:47.617 --> 43:50.800
so I'm truly thrilled.

710
43:50.800 --> 43:52.733
I look forward to working with you.

711
43:52.733 --> 43:55.913
Yes! I'll give it my best muscle!

712
43:55.913 --> 43:57.193
Oh, my.

713
43:57.193 --> 44:00.122
- Okay. - I love it!

714
44:00.122 --> 44:01.433
[Cynical Molco and Full Tummy Molco: The Movie]

715
44:01.433 --> 44:02.433
[Two Hearts Connected by Tuesla] Cute!

716
44:02.433 --> 44:04.929
- Wow, so cute! - Cute!

717
44:04.929 --> 44:07.966
One more...

718
44:07.966 --> 44:09.645
- Okay! - Yes, look over here!

719
44:09.645 --> 44:12.700
- Ready? Say, "Love!" - Love!

720
44:12.700 --> 44:14.533
- Love! - Love!

721
44:14.533 --> 44:16.621
- Cute! - So cute!

722
44:16.621 --> 44:18.893
- Thank you very much. - How about this one?

723
44:28.569 --> 44:30.373
How is it?

724
44:31.993 --> 44:34.149
Delicious.

725
44:34.149 --> 44:35.429
I love this.

726
44:35.429 --> 44:37.225
I see.

727
44:51.700 --> 44:53.966
I love it.

728
45:15.893 --> 45:19.717
I love Tuesla.

729
45:21.013 --> 45:23.458
- I'm truly grateful. - Yeah!

730
45:26.869 --> 45:28.629
I love it.

731
45:56.065 --> 46:01.476
[The End]
